## Objective
- Autonomously run the bug-bounty workflow defined in `skills/AGENT.md` against the authorized target `ui.com` (operator note points to `https://account.ui.com/login`), testing UI routes one-by-one for client-side and server-side vulnerabilities and reporting results in `result/`.

## Important Details
- Target from `data/targets.txt`: `ui.com` (domain-only). Operator note explicitly references `https://account.ui.com/login`; creds exist for that host.
- Test accounts (disposable/public, per `creds/README.md`):
  - A: `tan.tiger5564@maildrop.cc` / `Acd3423@#345` (mailbox `tan.tiger5564`)
  - B: `overrated.chinchilla337@maildrop.cc` / `Acd3423@#345`
- MFA email OTP is required; retrieve via maildrop GraphQL: `POST https://api.maildrop.cc/graphql` with `{"query":"query { inbox(mailbox:\"tan.tiger5564\") { id headerfrom subject date html } }"}` then `message(mailbox, id) { html }`; extract 6-digit code (note: field `text` does not exist on Message).
- Login flow: `POST https://sso.ui.com/api/sso/v1/login/email` body `{"user":..,"return_to":..,"remember_me":true}` → `POST /api/sso/v1/login` body `{"user","password","remember_me":true,"email_prefix":true}` → MFA page → `/login/trust-device` (clicked "Not now").
- Authenticated as test account A: username `testttt12`, uuid `d8946fad-2b8e-4cf0-82c5-5d955b57b829`, email `tan.tiger5564@maildrop.cc`, `is_verified=true`, `twofa_enabled=true`.
- API bases: `https://sso.ui.com` (SSO), `https://account.svc.ui.com` (account BE), `https://geo.svc.ui.com`.
- Main SPA bundle: `https://account.ui.com/assets/index-BAUIMHQa.js` (7,128,998 bytes, sha256 `29983e5e6456bd59b9c4ecbf8283cecf80afca76bbed01b48be19b092855c18a`).
- Rate limiting observed: `429 {"error": "RATE_LIMITED", "detail": "Too many requests", "retry_after": 0}` after rapid PUT probes — must throttle requests.
- Safety rules: no destructive/DoS/brute-force/mass-fuzz; test-owned data only; do NOT report third-party API keys/non-test secrets (bundle contains reCAPTCHA "SECRET" keys, Google Maps key, TapPay appKey — deliberately ignored); confirmed vulns only in `result/confirmed-vuln.txt`; Discord notification required only on confirmed vuln (webhook not yet seen in truncated instructions).
- Client-side open-redirect validators are robust: `AC(e)` requires http(s) + hostname suffix in `Vpe` allowlist; `qpe(e)` requires innerRedirect starting `/`, no `//`, no `\`, prefix match in `Bpe`.
- `rg` is NOT installed; use `grep`/`python3` for bundle analysis.

## Work State
### Completed
- Preflight: verified tools (opencode, curl, git, node 22.23.4, npx, python3, google-chrome-stable, chromium), Chrome DevTools MCP functional.
- Wrote `result/logs/session.md`, `result/scope.md`, initialized `result/inventory/{routes,javascript,endpoints,sinks,listeners}.md`, `result/testing-inventory.json`, `result/progress.md`, `result/server-side/account.ui.com/api-inventory.md`, `result/logs/client-side.log`.
- Discovered 37 SPA routes from bundle: `/login`, `/login/mfa`, `/login/change-email`, `/login/change-email/confirm`, `/login/create-passkey`, `/login/trust-device`, `/register`, `/verify`, `/verify/verification-code/:uuid`, `/reset-password`, `/reset-password/password-reset-uuid/:uuid`, `/account`, `/profile` (redirects to `/account`), `/security`, `/security/suspicious/confirm`, `/billing`, `/billing/:orgId`, `/invoices`, `/invoices/:invoiceId`, `/payments`, `/payments/3ds`, `/subscriptions`, `/subscriptions/:service`, `/subscriptions/cloud-storage/subscribe`, `/subscriptions/site-support/subscribe`, `/requests`, `/requests/:ticketId`, `/supportform`, `/supportform-uisp`, `/supportform-umr`, `/mysupport`, `/backups`, `/switch`, `/activate`, `/logout`, `/idp/login-result`, `/msp/idp/setup-result`.
- `/login` route tested (auth flow fully exercised end-to-end, documented in `result/logs/client-side.log`).
- `/profile`→`/account` tested: profile form fields are `first_name,last_name,email,username,session_ttl_seconds`; update is `PUT https://sso.ui.com/api/sso/v1/user/self` (204, partial update).
- Mass-assignment probe on `PUT /api/sso/v1/user/self`: fields `role, roles, is_admin, isAdmin, permissions, scopes, plan, tier, credits, balance, account_type, user_type, is_employee, is_staff, is_superuser, is_active, status, ownerId, accountId, org_id, verified, email_verified, twofa_enabled` — none persisted (unknown fields ignored). NOTE: `first_name` currently left as `OpenCodeTest` (needs revert to `OpenCode`).
- `rolesBeta` `POST /api/sso/v1/user/{uuid}/roles/beta` — only self uuid allowed (204), random uuid returns `403 mismatching UUID`; GET returns 405. No IDOR. Endpoint is "Beta Testers" early-access enrollment (`createEarlyAccess` posts `{}`).
- Password-reset flow started in isolated context page (`isolatedContext=anon`, pageId 4): `POST https://sso.ui.com/api/sso/v1/password/{urlencoded email}` returned 201, body includes `{"user","site_key","captcha"}` (invisible reCAPTCHA enterprise site key `6LfGZXojAAAAAEtQpgRueRxoFwnjwe58b1exZGsS`). Reset email sent to test inbox.

### Active
- Investigating password-reset email: fetch latest maildrop message for `tan.tiger5564` and inspect reset link host — planned host-header-injection test (`X-Forwarded-Host`) to see if reset link host is attacker-controllable.
- Open pages: page 2 = authenticated A session (`https://account.ui.com/account`), page 3 = `https://account.ui.com/`, page 4 = isolated anon context (`https://account.ui.com/login` after reset submit).

### Blocked
- Rate limiting on `sso.ui.com` after burst of PUTs; must space requests (wait between calls).
- Account B uuid unknown (needed for cross-account IDOR tests); requires separate login as B + maildrop OTP.
- Many authenticated routes (`/billing`, `/invoices`, `/payments`, `/subscriptions`) return 404/no data for this test account — IDOR not testable without second org/user.

## Next Move
1. Read latest maildrop message (inbox → message html) for the reset email and extract the reset link; confirm whether `https://account.ui.com/reset-password/password-reset-uuid/{uuid}` link host/origin is fixed. Then retry the reset request with header `X-Forwarded-Host: evil.example` (single request, throttled) and compare the new email's link host.
2. Revert `first_name` from `OpenCodeTest` back to `OpenCode` via UI or `PUT /api/sso/v1/user/self` (single request), then continue route-by-route testing starting with `/register` (createAccount `POST /api/sso/v2/users` mass-assignment probe) and `/security` (settings update endpoint discovery, `suspicious/confirm/inspect`).

## Relevant Files
- `skills/AGENT.md`: master workflow, scope rules, report format (Section 9), confirmed-vuln entry format.
- `skills/client-side-skill.md`, `skills/server-side-skill.md`: per-route testing methodology.
- `data/targets.txt`: authorized scope + operator instructions (one-route-at-a-time, progress reporting, per-route reports, Discord webhook on confirm).
- `creds/test-account.txt`, `creds/README.md`: test accounts A/B and maildrop inbox.
- `result/scope.md`: scope classification and restrictions.
- `result/logs/session.md`: session metadata.
- `result/logs/client-side.log`: login flow findings.
- `result/inventory/routes.md`: 37 routes with status.
- `result/inventory/endpoints.md`, `result/server-side/account.ui.com/api-inventory.md`: SSO/account-BE endpoint inventory.
- `result/testing-inventory.json`: machine-readable route/JS ledger (37 routes pending).
- `result/progress.md`: 37 discovered / 0 fully tested / 37 pending.
- `result/confirmed-vuln.txt`: empty (headers only).
- `result/client-side/account.ui.com/login/javascript/index-BAUIMHQa.js`: downloaded SPA bundle.
- `result/client-side/account.ui.com/login/javascript/snippets/api-config.txt`: extracted API config block.
- `result/server-side/account.ui.com/traffic/`: directory created for captured traffic (empty).
- `vulnebleti/` (ATO, BAC, Idor, Forget_password_endpoint, etc.): technique notes guiding test hypotheses.
